  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Women&#x2019;s Rights Programme in Kenya, implemented by ActionAid and local partners aims to increase access to economic opportunties and are benefitting from a safer and equal economic environment. . The main objective is for marginalised women to have increased control over financial decisions and feel safer when demanding their economic rights.  Objective: women access safer and a more equal economic environment (control over financial/ economic decision making ) Outcome: Marginalized women and survivors of GBV have increased access to economic opportunities and are benefitting from a safer and equal economic environment.</narrative>
  </description>
